# external_data — TRACK the fetch scripts + provenance so a fresh clone can rebuild the
# corpus (python external_data/fetch_all.py), but IGNORE the large, regeneratable data
# files themselves (SEC 10-Ks, EM-DAT xlsx, FRED CSVs, policy PDFs, Wikipedia txt,
# World Bank JSON, NOAA JSON, WGI xlsx, ...). Ignore by extension across all data dirs:
external_data/**/*.csv
external_data/**/*.xlsx
external_data/**/*.xls
external_data/**/*.html
external_data/**/*.pdf
external_data/**/*.zip
external_data/**/*.dat
external_data/**/*.json
external_data/**/*.txt
external_data/**/*.faiss
external_data/**/*.npz
external_data/**/*.parquet
# ...but always keep the tracked fetchers + provenance docs:
!external_data/*.py
!external_data/PROVENANCE.md
